  "footer_text": "ABOUT Careers Contact FAQ LEGAL INFORMATION Cookies notice Copyright and permissions Privacy notice Terms and conditions Warning on fraudulent schemes STAY CONNECTED SIGN UP TO RECEIVE EMAIL ALERTS BIS alerts",
  "above_fold_text": "About Research & publications Committees Speeches Statistics Media & events Search Home Research & publications Research & publications Quarterly Review The BIS Quarterly Review examines developments in international banking and financial markets. In March, September and December, it comprises a review of market developments over the past quarter, and articles that analyse topical economic and financial issues. The June edition will be published only when circumstances warrant. The June edition does not cover market developments given its proximity to the BIS Annual Economic Report. The views expressed in the Quarterly Reviews do not necessarily reflect the views of the BIS member central banks. On this page Recent issues Conventions used in the BIS Quarterly Review Welcome to the new BIS website. Please share your feedback to help us improve.",
  "visible_text": "Skip to main content\nAbout\nResearch & publications\nCommittees\nSpeeches\nStatistics\nMedia & events\nSearch\n \nHome\n Research & publications\nResearch & publications\nQuarterly Review\n\nThe BIS Quarterly Review examines developments in international banking and financial markets. In March, September and December, it comprises a review of market developments over the past quarter, and articles that analyse topical economic and financial issues. The June edition will be published only when circumstances warrant. The June edition does not cover market developments given its proximity to the BIS Annual Economic Report.\n\nThe views expressed in the Quarterly Reviews do not necessarily reflect the views of the BIS member central banks.\n\n \n \nOn this page\nRecent issues\nConventions used in the BIS Quarterly Review\nRecent issues\nQuarterly Review\n14 Sep 2026\nBIS Quarterly Review, September 2026\nQuarterly Review\n15 Jun 2026\nBIS Quarterly Review, June 2026\nQuarterly Review\n16 Mar 2026\nBIS Quarterly Review, March 2026\nQuarterly Review\n8 Dec 2025\nBIS Quarterly Review, December 2025\nQuarterly Review\n15 Sep 2025\nBIS Quarterly Review, September 2025\nQuarterly Review\n11 Mar 2025\nBIS Quarterly Review, March 2025\nThe March issue of the BIS Quarterly Review includes analysis on developments in financial markets, private credit, the…\nQuarterly Review\n10 Dec 2024\nBIS Quarterly Review, December 2024\nQuarterly Review\n16 Sep 2024\nBIS Quarterly Review, September 2024\nQuarterly Review\n10 Jun 2024\nBIS Quarterly Review, June 2024\nQuarterly Review\n4 Mar 2024\nBIS Quarterly Review, March 2024\nQuarterly Review\n4 Dec 2023\nBIS Quarterly Review, December 2023\nQuarterly Review\n18 Sep 2023\nBIS Quarterly Review, September 2023\nQuarterly Review\n27 Feb 2023\nBIS Quarterly Review, March 2023\nQuarterly Review\n5 Dec 2022\nBIS Quarterly Review, December 2022\nQuarterly Review\n19 Sep 2022\nBIS Quarterly Review, September 2022\nSee all\nConventions used in the BIS Quarterly Review\ne\testimated\nlhs, rhs\tleft-hand side, right-hand side\nbillion\tthousand million\n...\tnot available\n.\tnot applicable\n-\tnil or negligible\n$\tUS dollar unless specified otherwise\n\nDifferences in totals are due to rounding.\n\nThe term \"country\" as used in this publication also covers territorial entities that are not states as understood by international law and practice but for which data are separately and independently maintained.\n\nCurrency codes\nCountry codes\nYou might also be interested in\nDISCOVER\nAnnual report\nLEARN MORE\nBIS authors\nDISCOVER\nPublications in peer-reviewed journals\nABOUT\nCareers\nContact\nFAQ\nLEGAL INFORMATION\nCookies notice\nCopyright and permissions\nPrivacy notice\nTerms and conditions\nWarning on fraudulent schemes\nSTAY CONNECTED\nSIGN UP TO RECEIVE EMAIL ALERTS\nBIS alerts\nWelcome to the new BIS website. Please share your feedback to help us improve.",
